      "n_chars": 39,
      "section": "frontmatter",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Introduction}\\label{sec:intro}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0012",
      "sha256": "daef2ca93399e0022bdc5ecb4b7067462762ebaa8dc78c92b3d5cc94eb684fc4",
      "char_start": 2913,
      "char_end": 3390,
      "n_chars": 477,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Most machine-learning work on the electrocardiogram (ECG) is supervised, but the"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0013",
      "sha256": "ffddd8a0ac74561bcc76286218b9abd33f103612bda33d55d386e5dcfeedf200",
      "char_start": 3392,
      "char_end": 4056,
      "n_chars": 664,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "This study began as a re-examination of a master's project that clustered whole"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0014",
      "sha256": "9cbb5970197f0529258684f3187517a7fced1795a529f576d40f0f0384139057",
      "char_start": 4058,
      "char_end": 4688,
      "n_chars": 630,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "A representation can carry information about a label and still fail to cluster by it."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0015",
      "sha256": "befad9901509bc41823158e2f1eae5e2125d965ac73cd3a4082ccb9f2e22482a",
      "char_start": 4690,
      "char_end": 5234,
      "n_chars": 544,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The most directly related work benchmarks several ECG foundation models against one"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0016",
      "sha256": "cc636608051e7826a2508904ea85db9e89a7a11eff749bdb95e4dd7a0b5c1ff1",
      "char_start": 5236,
      "char_end": 6766,
      "n_chars": 1530,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We therefore benchmark four representation families for unsupervised SR-versus-AF"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0017",
      "sha256": "4afdec2dfaa41e91e84c8aeb37b136759effc3da5decf940f5cf2292f405ecda",
      "char_start": 6768,
      "char_end": 6809,
      "n_chars": 41,
      "section": "Introduction",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Related work}\\label{sec:related}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0018",
      "sha256": "7a1ef2581a81ea93308a57138ce4ed06c23ed9107ce96e9c183c660b1d7da851",
      "char_start": 6811,
      "char_end": 8239,
      "n_chars": 1428,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Unsupervised ECG and representations.} Hand-crafted features built from"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0019",
      "sha256": "d1e989b560d85900095a9965f76df0695a4045f59142b5a465453850900250df",
      "char_start": 8241,
      "char_end": 8830,
      "n_chars": 589,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Clustering evaluation.} Cluster purity is not chance-corrected: assigning"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0020",
      "sha256": "2b70e0522ad410121920b5d476fc9f1b668d385b5fdd72231c5bf5f6f441ddc4",
      "char_start": 8832,
      "char_end": 9417,
      "n_chars": 585,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{Closest benchmark.} The ECG foundation-model benchmark of"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0021",
      "sha256": "58f73a85115cb870e9c901e9dc70be0c59b3ecfc2021a0b4dab3e2b59b522dd0",
      "char_start": 9419,
      "char_end": 9455,
      "n_chars": 36,
      "section": "Related work",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Methods}\\label{sec:methods}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0022",
      "sha256": "60e22f7e5d82d55f9882d00071eacee46dd55348b1c7a5117f04b8002a89a680",
      "char_start": 9457,
      "char_end": 9486,
      "n_chars": 29,
      "section": "Methods",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Data and cohorts}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0023",
      "sha256": "9000f7612e6ed4319861422b49a208e2bc34e28d17966639afaf6b97a8c8fa54",
      "char_start": 9488,
      "char_end": 10262,
      "n_chars": 774,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{PTB-XL.} We use PTB-XL \\cite{ptbxl2020}, a public 12-lead database"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0024",
      "sha256": "a6d9b8dc99a8b3608dd877ee7c8d1b06d58c00d3cc379ba388028532f2fa3085",
      "char_start": 10264,
      "char_end": 10719,
      "n_chars": 455,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\paragraph{MIT-BIH.} For generalization we use the MIT-BIH Arrhythmia Database"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0025",
      "sha256": "0667ca2d8823bd258eac972c1cb93634e277f43d22fae54fb5c99d5de9e57121",
      "char_start": 10721,
      "char_end": 10749,
      "n_chars": 28,
      "section": "Data and cohorts",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Representations}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0026",
      "sha256": "1571603e7d574e260e37d95213491e60eadd8e27307c5e01dd3c776dfd4f53a3",
      "char_start": 10751,
      "char_end": 12268,
      "n_chars": 1517,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We compare four families on PTB-XL (Table~\\ref{tab:main}):"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0027",
      "sha256": "c1d86f92ac925d37322caa54832aa4f2d5dad14a4fa67ae6501eca2904d4c327",
      "char_start": 12270,
      "char_end": 12308,
      "n_chars": 38,
      "section": "Representations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Clustering and evaluation}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0028",
      "sha256": "c9a21951fb1ac82d24c8a3e14e9e31fef94007775543787e809e8d4225489249",
      "char_start": 12310,
      "char_end": 13859,
      "n_chars": 1549,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Each representation is clustered with $k$-means, Ward agglomerative, spectral,"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0029",
      "sha256": "b0f1ebbaa1c94fdf5c444a81ef1d03e772f57d4bc99100bf1997ccff18d2d582",
      "char_start": 13861,
      "char_end": 13894,
      "n_chars": 33,
      "section": "Clustering and evaluation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Federated robustness}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0030",
      "sha256": "5d50604bca1cb398d8d202ef28b22908969058cbcd757cc691519c640de097a0",
      "char_start": 13896,
      "char_end": 14421,
      "n_chars": 525,
      "section": "Federated robustness",
      "first_line_excerpt": "To probe deployment under data siloing we use standard federated $k$-means with"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0031",
      "sha256": "38af922a42eab1675171bc8e32009b028472bf2fc5bbc7d98f5ff5312845354b",
      "char_start": 14423,
      "char_end": 14459,
      "n_chars": 36,
      "section": "Federated robustness",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Results}\\label{sec:results}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0032",
      "sha256": "bc883d7f1ced945675d7a74862a2a099007e960a29e80ff32e14a4988c7b4a8b",
      "char_start": 14461,
      "char_end": 14527,
      "n_chars": 66,
      "section": "Results",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0033",
      "sha256": "cdbf268c69562429297eb39201f371e5e0e9f458be7c75a95551fc61f78f7a64",
      "char_start": 14529,
      "char_end": 15041,
      "n_chars": 512,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Table~\\ref{tab:main} and Fig.~\\ref{fig:heatmap} summarise the PTB-XL benchmark."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0034",
      "sha256": "5022644e3146ebb091714fdd191586e67208d98d5b4c05c401413b6ebdb2f27a",
      "char_start": 15043,
      "char_end": 16120,
      "n_chars": 1077,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0035",
      "sha256": "c346ce08605ad822408429b737249619f80eaa6bce55e9adb64650d0d2a3e40b",
      "char_start": 16122,
      "char_end": 16342,
      "n_chars": 220,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0036",
      "sha256": "297537cae8b99be47f24b3108fea881be98d962579dc2040bebbcad1dc672760",
      "char_start": 16344,
      "char_end": 17126,
      "n_chars": 782,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Across ten seeds the partitional solutions are stable (standard deviation $\\le 0.001$ for"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0037",
      "sha256": "9452239fd88ab670c9326b91e490262e392a940b79448d44aa37278fda631463",
      "char_start": 17128,
      "char_end": 17670,
      "n_chars": 542,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The two foundation models do not behave as one category. ECGFounder clusters strongly while"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0038",
      "sha256": "ef6f5eb701fcd5b77c748c7598a8adc3cb8a57d402b192a360e8f10fe524facf",
      "char_start": 17672,
      "char_end": 17719,
      "n_chars": 47,
      "section": "Representation, not algorithm, governs clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Separability is not clusterability}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0039",
      "sha256": "07787834cf1d1b55f5d9730ddaa551fda500510d1124b9985009f09e70926427",
      "char_start": 17721,
      "char_end": 18788,
      "n_chars": 1067,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The supervised ceilings (last column of Table~\\ref{tab:main}; Fig.~\\ref{fig:sep})"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0040",
      "sha256": "59f04ada4db0c6aa1b32d0d2f227a28dc93b9653ede9704ba03858c09848e57a",
      "char_start": 18790,
      "char_end": 19089,
      "n_chars": 299,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0041",
      "sha256": "b3eb476ff58189ffd6535514e14b0a4144a30aa0d3d2711f3e346b848b326a4d",
      "char_start": 19091,
      "char_end": 19123,
      "n_chars": 32,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{The silhouette trap}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0042",
      "sha256": "1c7ae8f3f6741f6495746db0bb96401a49d1c096c4e483b9af545643593c0cdd",
      "char_start": 19125,
      "char_end": 19807,
      "n_chars": 682,
      "section": "The silhouette trap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Internal indices mislead here in a specific, reproducible way. Raw flattening with"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0043",
      "sha256": "2b44c324b7cbcb6b51a6bd8e7b9b7d37e983464e9a954218aa6e1896de20db4a",
      "char_start": 19809,
      "char_end": 20171,
      "n_chars": 362,
      "section": "The silhouette trap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0044",
      "sha256": "493e7a36c1189e4ca8ab27705114ffbebc0dc4c4120810c6aea4efb4b42b17d9",
      "char_start": 20173,
      "char_end": 20206,
      "n_chars": 33,
      "section": "The silhouette trap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Conditioning matters}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0045",
      "sha256": "87c2176f8396d24cd2471024d32ef3a6f6d85b39f3970828245b6f3cd1ec0ac7",
      "char_start": 20208,
      "char_end": 20818,
      "n_chars": 610,
      "section": "Conditioning matters",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The feature scaler changes the outcome materially. For the hand-crafted features the"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0046",
      "sha256": "d1aa75eab2439ed71ffd4dec4e8d3b02470fd1326598961e3db50a32ffc48ad2",
      "char_start": 20820,
      "char_end": 20874,
      "n_chars": 54,
      "section": "Conditioning matters",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Generalization to MIT-BIH beat morphology}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0047",
      "sha256": "affa6c06066abb0eb5953d12e7897ea58a48ec1ed2abe38d0f59dde6f1de509e",
      "char_start": 20876,
      "char_end": 21419,
      "n_chars": 543,
      "section": "Generalization to MIT-BIH beat morphology",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The ordering replicates on a different dataset and a different task type"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0048",
      "sha256": "c92442fb83cfdda3ab3c1d09c33e11c761b42b012a3f5022cf2e43e6623b530c",
      "char_start": 21421,
      "char_end": 21969,
      "n_chars": 548,
      "section": "Generalization to MIT-BIH beat morphology",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0049",
      "sha256": "c57fe02701a2cdb4fc8c105016411ffbbd2346b2f5cca0ce2f7c18da888059da",
      "char_start": 21971,
      "char_end": 22044,
      "n_chars": 73,
      "section": "Generalization to MIT-BIH beat morphology",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0050",
      "sha256": "b9c5c2875df1baed6745c16472336b3ae651eb06aa391cf271cdfa57b061f175",
      "char_start": 22046,
      "char_end": 22636,
      "n_chars": 590,
      "section": "Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Two stressors closer to deployment separate the representations more sharply than the"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "sha256": "7a453d4fef66ef6c817f7ee03332df932c76ca48865ab0ef9ea8ab1d590f330c",
      "char_start": 22638,
      "char_end": 23375,
      "n_chars": 737,
      "section": "Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Second, federation. Under IID federation across ten sites, every representation retains"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "sha256": "595279f7af2c3d6e85e05ce00a240674052be542d8a708c1e9dc165e9f5a4f75",
      "char_start": 23377,
      "char_end": 23910,
      "n_chars": 533,
      "section": "Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0053",
      "sha256": "366d443e6e0026559b437b0a6ec576de27e641b0ece433facaf211b92a29fa86",
      "char_start": 23912,
      "char_end": 24201,
      "n_chars": 289,
      "section": "Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0054",
      "sha256": "0e561cd228c334147de30c33ea5b097837393c0eea887bc74293d1ce48f72b7c",
      "char_start": 24203,
      "char_end": 24245,
      "n_chars": 42,
      "section": "Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Discussion}\\label{sec:discussion}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0055",
      "sha256": "daf691274d3f7a4647345fe170ce9b2d4f9a2b108908a088a49396547743d2bf",
      "char_start": 24247,
      "char_end": 25182,
      "n_chars": 935,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The practical reading is a decision rule. If a strong public foundation model can be run"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0056",
      "sha256": "4ee760ab90a76ebab5668e358cd8dd710772fe808a6ab3a639be3c50d4754f10",
      "char_start": 25184,
      "char_end": 25618,
      "n_chars": 434,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The result also reframes the original master's project honestly. Its conclusion that the"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "sha256": "1bef00aec08ee0341f751d74d5ab5f04ff9378db2284c440d875ca60b0928c45",
      "char_start": 25620,
      "char_end": 26228,
      "n_chars": 608,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We claim no methodological novelty. The separability-versus-clusterability phenomenon is"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0058",
      "sha256": "afaa0b7efcda8f9ead6b600c7b846ef2de31476b8cf28f0710776b2932380b7a",
      "char_start": 26230,
      "char_end": 26274,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Limitations}\\label{sec:limitations}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0059",
      "sha256": "d717edbf9310d5dd955240097e4eaea5548917ae2e121c34e4824e13567fa8c4",
      "char_start": 26276,
      "char_end": 27355,
      "n_chars": 1079,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "ECGFounder expects 500\\,Hz input, and because bulk streaming of the 500\\,Hz records was"
    },
